DevOps Interview Preparation
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 2
Git & GitHub (Advanced + Real-World Usage)

At 2–4 years, interviewers expect you to:

Work confidently with teams

Handle merge conflicts

Follow branching strategies

Use Git in CI/CD & GitOps workflows

🔹 Git Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Difference between git fetch and git pull
• git rebase vs git merge — when do you use which?
• What is a detached HEAD state?
• How do you resolve merge conflicts?
• Explain Git branching strategies (GitFlow, Trunk-based)
• How do you revert a commit already pushed to remote?
• Difference between git reset --soft, --mixed, --hard
• What is git cherry-pick and its use case?
• How do you squash commits and why?
• How do you tag releases in Git?
• What are hooks in Git?
• How do you maintain clean commit history?
• How do you handle secrets in Git repositories?

🔹 GitHub Interview Questions

• GitHub vs GitLab vs Bitbucket
• What are protected branches?
• What are pull request best practices?
• How do code reviews improve quality?
• What is GitHub Actions?
• How does GitHub Actions integrate with CI/CD?
• How do you secure GitHub repositories?
• What are GitHub environments?
• How do you manage secrets in GitHub?
• What is GitOps?
• GitHub + Kubernetes GitOps flow (high level)

🔹 Real-World Scenarios

• Accidentally pushed wrong code to main — what will you do?
• Multiple developers modifying the same file — how do you handle it?
• Pipeline triggered on every commit — how do you optimize it?
• How do you enforce quality checks before merge?
• How do you rollback a release using Git?

 Interview Tip:
Say this confidently:

👉 “We use feature branches, PR reviews, protected main branch, and CI checks before merge.”
